{"ts":"2026-08-30T21:39:59.317Z","author":"codex","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"ea5856882c73d923eca2015a","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-web-ccie"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Offline mutation queue is not bound to the originating account or idempotency key"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Offline API mutations are stored with method, path, and body but no authenticated user identity or idempotency key. If a browser changes accounts before reconnecting, replay uses the current session; if a response is lost after the server commits, retry can repeat a non-idempotent mutation. The CSRF work in pm-web-413z deliberately repairs token freshness without pretending to solve account ownership or exactly-once delivery."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":0},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["idempotency","multi-user","offline","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-30T21:39:59.317Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-30T21:39:59.317Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Every queued mutation is durably bound to the authenticated user/session that created it; a different account never replays it; unknown legacy ownership is preserved and surfaced for explicit recovery without blocking unrelated owned records; every mutation carries a server-enforced idempotency key so retry after an ambiguous response cannot duplicate state; real browser/service-worker/PostgreSQL tests cover logout/login, account switching, lost responses, restart, queue ordering, and zero data loss."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The CSRF review proved queue records survive browser sessions and surfaced the adjacent cross-account and ambiguous-retry risks; multi-user production readiness requires explicit ownership and exactly-once semantics."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reviewer","value":"security-review"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"pm-web 2026.8.29 offline service-worker queue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Queue a mutation while authenticated as user A, change the browser session to user B before reconnecting, then flush; the request is authenticated as B. Separately, let the server commit a non-idempotent mutation but drop the response; the retained record retries without an idempotency key."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Queued work remains owned by its creator and ambiguous retries are exactly-once."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Replay uses whichever session is current and has no deduplication identity."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.8.29"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"Offline mutation queue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"A shared browser can attribute pending work to the wrong user, and a network ambiguity can duplicate mutations."}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"29cd8a4b05536868e1268113d1b11a0891af96eb17d7808f644133eb2df11c94","item_hash_version":2,"message":"Track account binding and exactly-once replay separately from CSRF token freshness"}
